  "lineage": "Recitation of the gabay, the most prestigious and formally demanding genre of Somali oral poetry — long, alliterative, quantitative-metre verse on weighty themes of politics, philosophy, war and reconciliation, composed by a named poet (abwaan) and transmitted verbatim by memoriser-reciters. Central to Somali public life across the Horn of Africa, the tradition produced figures such as Sayyid Mohammed Abdullah Hassan and sustained the twentieth-century 'chain' poem-debates (silsilad); every line must alliterate on a chosen consonant throughout the poem. Delivery is grave, measured, elevated speech in which the poem's argument and its exact wording carry the art.",
